    {
      "jobId": "78c16471-f714-4e82-bbee-27f1afce54e7",
      "question": "Which loan product had the highest 30-day delinquency rate in September 2026, and how does each product compare with September 2025?",
      "submittedAt": "2026-10-04T05:32:24.795371Z",
      "completedAt": "2026-10-04T05:32:32.488309Z",
      "status": "success",
      "report": {
        "markdown": "**September 2026: Auto loans had the highest 30-day delinquency rate at 4.78%.**\n\n| Product | Sep 2025 | Sep 2026 | Change (pp) |\n|---------|----------|----------|-------------|\n| Auto    | 1.37% (2/146) | 4.78% (12/251) | +3.41 |\n| Personal| 2.99% (4/134) | 3.35% (7/209)  | +0.36 |\n| Mortgage| 0.75% (1/133) | 3.01% (4/133)  | +2.26 |\n\nAll three products saw higher delinquency rates in September 2026 versus September 2025. Auto loans showed the largest increase (+3.41 pp) and overtook personal loans as the highest-risk product. Mortgage delinquency rose sharply despite a flat active-loan count, while personal loans grew in volume with only a modest rate increase. [1]\n\n## Sources\n\n- [1] Structured retrieval result — financial_services_banking — evidence `hermes-receipt:cb9f40d6ac3b948181c44ab425bde6d1f954d2de228d9bef948a3c5680dfd25d`",
